  "narrative": "The conditional persistence analyses are now essentially complete and strongly support the four accepted dataset-specific associations. feature_037=1, feature_002=1, and feature_010=1 each remain large when feature_027 and the other two accepted markers are absent (signed estimates 0.44-0.81, all lower bounds well above 0.15), so I accept H128-H130 and close these tests. These are association claims within the supplied dataset, not causal independence claims. The new interaction tests do not support effect modification: feature_063-by-feature_010 is not threshold supported (H123/H132), and feature_037-by-feature_040 median split is not threshold supported (H133/H134). Broad screens for feature_028, feature_013, feature_034 level_002 vs level_001, and feature_054 level_003 vs level_001 are null, and feature_062 level_003 vs level_002 is invalid due only 13 observations in one cell. feature_063 remains the only borderline line. H112's independent validation interval is directionally consistent but its lower bound is below threshold, so I reject/close H112 itself. The newer conditional claims H121, H122, and H131 have 95% lower bounds above threshold, but this pattern emerged from multiple nested subgroup tests and H112 already failed strict validation. I therefore do not accept feature_063 yet. I request independent validation for H122 because it is the most powered new threshold-crossing conditional claim and tests feature_063 when feature_002 and feature_010 are absent; H131 is cleaner but smaller, and H121 is less specific. If H122 validation supports the threshold, feature_063 can be reconsidered as a subgroup-specific dataset association; if it fails, I will likely close feature_063 absent a separate compelling validation of H131.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 appraise. Accepted dataset-specific associations: feature_037=1 lower outcome_001, feature_027=1 lower outcome_001, feature_002=1 higher outcome_001, feature_010=1 higher outcome_001. Mutual-persistence screen complete: feature_027 persists when the accepted trio is absent (H108-H111), and feature_037/feature_002/feature_010 persist when the other three accepted markers, including feature_027, are absent (H128-H130). feature_003 closed as not threshold supported. feature_063 unresolved: all-cohort H83 lower bound below threshold; selected conditional H121/H122/H131 discovery lower bounds above threshold, but H112 validation lower bound below threshold and interaction H123/H132 does not support effect modification. H112 rejected due failed validation uncertainty. H121 deferred. H131 active but smaller/cleaner. Requested validation for H122 (feature_002=0 and feature_010=0) as the most powered new conditional threshold test. If validation passes threshold, consider accepting H122 and decide whether H121/H131 deserve separate validation; if validation fails, close feature_063 unless H131 is independently compelling. New nulls: feature_028, feature_013, feature_034 level_002 vs level_001, feature_054 level_003 vs level_001, feature_062 invalid due cell_n, feature_040 median-split modification of feature_037. Remaining untested/unresolved: H107 feature_061 level contrast; H135/H136 feature_054 level_003 vs level_002; optional other categorical contrasts. Interpret all accepted associations as dataset-specific only, without causal or external generalizability claims.",
